  "description": "02 §9.6 played out instead of asserted: thick lines, thin junction. A 250 MW junction sits mid-corridor between Modrzyca and Jasienica, with three MV lines of 500 MW meeting at it. Jasienica connects on turn 14 and its 490–630 MW demand can only be served through the junction: delivery pins at ~250 MW plus Modrzyca's own supply and ENS runs 50–324 MW per turn. Day 3 wires in the second CCGT (500 MW) — offered power goes to 650 MW, delivery does not move, and the surplus setpoints turn into 230–343 MW of dump: more generation does not fix a station. The capacity module ordered the same day lands on day 4 (throughput 500 MW) and ENS collapses to 0–61 MW.",
